{%- comment -%}
  TIKVES LONDON . HEAD CSS
  28 Sep 2026, speed. Layout rules that must be in place before the page
  first paints. Rendered from layout/theme.liquid straight after theme.css.

  Why here and not in a footer section: a footer section arrives at the end
  of the HTML. On a slow connection the phone painted the collection grid in
  the theme's two columns first, then this rule arrived and flipped it to
  one, and everything below jumped by a whole card. Measured 28 Sep 2026 as
  a layout shift of 0.37 on all-wines, failing Google's limit.

  Colour and popup styling can stay in footer sections. Anything that moves
  content belongs here.

  ONE PER ROW ON MOBILE. Operator ruling 6 Sep 2026: on a phone a collection
  page shows one bottle per row, not two, so the card, its descriptor line,
  its price and its Add to cart button all read at full size. Desktop is
  untouched. Moved here from sections/tikves-one-per-row.liquid, which now
  renders nothing.

  CARDS CENTRED. Operator ruling 28 Sep 2026: on every product card the
  title, descriptor line, price and Add to cart button sit centred, on
  phone and desktop. The button's own size lives in
  snippets/tikves-grid-add-to-cart.liquid. To undo, delete the second
  style block below.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% style %}
  @media only screen and (max-width: 768px) {
    .collection-grid .grid-product,
    .collection__grid .grid-product,
    .grid--uniform .grid-product,
    .product-grid .grid-product,
    .grid .grid-product {
      width: 100% !important;
      max-width: 100% !important;
      flex: 0 0 100% !important;
      clear: both !important;
      margin-bottom: 28px !important;
    }
    .grid-product .grid-product__content {
      max-width: 520px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .grid-product .grid-product__title {
      font-size: 20px !important;
    }
    /* 18 Oct 2026: the rule above also caught the swipe rows on a product
       page ("You may also like", "Recently viewed"), showing one card with
       no sign of the next. In those rows a card takes 78% so the next one
       peeks in. Collection and search grids are untouched. */
    /* 18 Oct 2026: the quantity - and + measured 30px on a phone, below a
       comfortable tap. Widen the box so each button is a 40px target. */
    .js-qty__wrapper,
    .drawer .js-qty__wrapper {
      max-width: 124px !important;
      min-width: 124px !important;
    }
    .js-qty__num,
    .drawer .js-qty__num {
      min-height: 40px;
      padding-left: 40px !important;
      padding-right: 40px !important;
    }
    .js-qty__adjust {
      width: 40px;
      padding: 0 !important;
    }
    .grid-overflow-wrapper .grid .grid-product {
      width: 78% !important;
      max-width: 78% !important;
      flex: 0 0 78% !important;
      clear: none !important;
      margin-bottom: 0 !important;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

{% style %}
  .grid-product .grid-product__content,
  .grid-product .grid-product__meta,
  .grid-product .tk-gatc {
    text-align: center;
  }
{% endstyle %}

{%- comment -%}
  AGE GATE FIRST, THEN COOKIES. Operator ruling 28 Sep 2026. While the age
  gate is open, Shopify's cookie banner stays hidden, so a first visit asks
  one question at a time. When the visitor answers Yes the gate closes and
  the banner appears as normal. Nothing optional loads before cookie consent
  either way. To undo, delete the style block below.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% style %}
  html:has(age-verification-popup.modal--is-active) #shopify-pc__banner {
    display: none !important;
  }
{% endstyle %}

{%- comment -%}
  COMPACT COOKIE BANNER ON PHONES. 18 Oct 2026, operator request. On a
  phone the banner filled the bottom 353px and covered Add to cart. Same
  words, same three buttons; Accept all and Reject all now sit side by
  side at equal size (44px tall), Choose cookies below them. About 240px
  tall on an iPhone 13. Desktop unchanged. To undo, delete the style
  block below.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% style %}
  @media only screen and (max-width: 768px) {
    #shopify-pc__banner.shopify-pc__banner__dialog { padding: 16px 16px calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) !important; }
    #shopify-pc__banner .shopify-pc__banner__wrapper { gap: 12px !important; }
    #shopify-pc__banner #shopify-pc__banner__body-title { font-size: 16px !important; margin: 0 0 4px !important; }
    #shopify-pc__banner .shopify-pc__banner__body p { font-size: 13px !important; line-height: 1.45 !important; margin: 0 !important; }
    #shopify-pc__banner .shopify-pc__banner__btns { flex-direction: row !important; flex-wrap: wrap !important; gap: 8px !important; margin: 0 !important; }
    #shopify-pc__banner #shopify-pc__banner__btn-accept,
    #shopify-pc__banner #shopify-pc__banner__btn-decline { flex: 1 1 0 !important; width: auto !important; min-width: 0 !important; min-height: 44px !important; margin: 0 !important; padding: 8px 10px !important; }
    #shopify-pc__banner #shopify-pc__banner__btn-accept { order: 1 !important; }
    #shopify-pc__banner #shopify-pc__banner__btn-decline { order: 2 !important; }
    #shopify-pc__banner #shopify-pc__banner__btn-manage-prefs { order: 3 !important; flex: 1 1 100% !important; width: 100% !important; min-height: 36px !important; margin: 0 !important; padding: 6px !important; }
  }
{% endstyle %}

{%- comment -%}
  ONE POP-UP AT A TIME. Operator ruling 17 Oct 2026, revised 18 Oct 2026.
  The second-page rule is gone: the sign-up pop-up can show on the first
  page. It never shows over the age gate, the cookie banner, a drawer or
  another modal, and it waits the full delay (popup_seconds in
  sections/popup-group.json, 15) after the last of those is answered or
  closed. The waiting lives in theme.NewsletterPopup in assets/theme.js.
{%- endcomment -%}
